  "name": "leptos",
  "description": "Leptos is a high-performance, full-stack Rust web framework that utilizes fine-grained reactivity to construct declarative user interfaces without the overhead of a virtual DOM. It facilitates isomorphic application development through server functions and robust support for various rendering modes, including client-side rendering, server-side rendering, and hydration with out-of-order streaming. The framework architecture leverages reactive primitives to ensure minimal runtime overhead by compiling component logic into direct, targeted DOM updates.",
